te individuals within the science education program of the students (MNE, 2018).\" refs W12.\n28. \"The document states that science literacy requires individuals to understand and use the scientific concepts in the social, cultural, economic and decision-making process.\" refs W12.\n29. \"The document states that one of the important dimensions of science literacy is to learn the scientific concepts.\" refs W12.\n30. \"The document states that concept learning is important in creating scientific principles by classifying the structures with similar characteristics and associating them with other concepts (Çepni et al., 1997).\" refs W12.\n31. \"The document states that in today's understanding, teaching of the Science course is based on making the information meaningful and experiential for the students rather than the evaluation of the student's level of knowledge (MNE, 2018).\" refs W12.\n32. \"The document states that the most important aim of the Science course is to train students to be science-literate.\" refs W12.\n\nThat's 32. Good. But note fact 11 and 12 could be combined. Also we didn't include Mehmet Diyaddin Yaşar's affiliation explicitly. But that's okay.\n\nCheck JSON validity. Need all strings properly escaped. Fact 6: title with apostrophe? \"Prospective Teachers' Creative Comparisons\" contains apostrophe. In JSON string, apostrophe is fine. No double quotes inside. Fact 13: citation with \"science education\" inside double quotes? I removed. Let's write: \"The document gives a citation for Yılmaz, Z. A., & Yaşar, M. D. (2022) in International Journal of Scholars in Education, 5(2), 101-116.\" No double quotes. Fact 8: \"Zeynel Abidin Yılmaz is listed as an Assoc. Prof. Dr. at Kilis 7 Aralık University.\" Good.\n\nFact 14: \"The abstract states that determination of prospective teachers' metaphoric perceptions of science education will contribute to the more effective and efficient organization of science education and the organization and structu